ontractors and agents from any claim, loss, liability, damage, cost or expense (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your use of the Services, your content, your transactions, your breach of these Terms or your violation of any law or of anyone's rights.")),c("22. Dispute resolution, arbitration and class action waiver",i({text:"Informal resolution.",strong:!0}," Before starting arbitration, you agree to email ",{text:"info@boithebear.com",href:"mailto:info@boithebear.com"}," with a description of your claim and to try in good faith to resolve it with us for at least 30 days."),i({text:"Binding arbitration.",strong:!0}," Any dispute, claim or controversy arising from or relating to the Services or these Terms will be resolved by final and binding individual arbitration administered by the American Arbitration Association under its Consumer Arbitration Rules (or its Commercial Arbitration Rules if you are not a consumer), before a single arbitrator. The arbitration may be held remotely; any in person hearing will take place in Wilmington, Delaware, unless the arbitrator decides otherwise. Judgment on the award may be entered in any court with jurisdiction."),i({text:"Exceptions.",strong:!0}," Either party may bring an individual claim in small claims court, and either party may seek injunctive relief in court to protect its intellectual property or to stop unauthorized access to the Services."),i({text:"Class action and jury waiver.",strong:!0}," You and BOI may bring claims only in an individual capacity, not as a plaintiff or class member in any class, collective or representative proceeding. The arbitrator may not consolidate claims or preside over any form of representative proceeding. You and BOI waive any right to a jury trial."),i({text:"Opt out.",strong:!0}," You may opt out of this Section 22 by emailing ",{text:"info@boithebear.com",href:"mailto:info@boithebear.com"},' with the subject "Arbitration opt out" within 30 days after you first accept these Terms, stating your name and the X or Google account you use with BOI.'),i({text:"Time limit.",strong:!0}," To the extent permitted by law, any claim must be brought within one year after it arises, or it is permanently barred.")),c("23. Governing law",i("These Terms and any dispute between you and BOI are governed by the laws of the State of Delaware and applicable United States federal law, without regard to conflict of law rules. Subject to Section 22, the state and federal courts located in Delaware have exclusive jurisdiction, and you consent to their jurisdiction.")),c("24. General",i("These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy and Risk Disclosure, are the entire agreement between you and BOI about the Services. If any part is found unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. Our failure to enforce a right is not a waiver. You may not assign these Terms without our consent; we may assign them, including in connection with a merger, acquisition, reorganization, change of name or brand, or sale of assets. We are not liable for delays or failures caused by events beyond our reasonable control. Sections that by their nature should survive termination will survive.")),c("25. Contact",i("Questions about these Terms can be sent to BoiTheBear LLC, 8 The Green, Suite B, Dover, Delaware 19901, United States, or by email to ",{text:"info@boithebear.com",href:"mailto:info@boithebear.com"},". Our official website is ",{text:"www.boithebear.com",href:"/"}," and our official X account is ",{text:"@boithebear",href:"https://x.com/boithebear"},"."))]},privacy:{title:"Privacy Policy",meta:[{label:"Last Updated",value:"October 8, 2026"}],intro:[i('This Privacy Policy explains how BoiTheBear LLC ("BOI", "we", "us" or "our") collects, uses, shares and protects personal information when you use www.boithebear.com and our related services (the "Services"). It should be read together with our ',{text:"Terms of Service",href:"/terms"},"."),i("BOI is a social platform built around public blockchains. Much of what you do on BOI, such as your profile, posts and on-chain transactions, is public by design. Please keep this in mind when you use the Services.")],sections:[c("1. Information you give us or that comes from your sign-in",s([{text:"X account information.",strong:!0}," When you sign in with X, we receive your X user ID, username (handle), display name, profile image, profile description and follower count. We store your X user ID, handle, profile image, follower count and, when your profile is first created, your profile description. We do not receive your X password or your email address, and we do not keep your X access token after sign-in."],[{text:"Google account information.",strong:!0}," Where Google sign-in is offered, we receive confirmation of your Google identity and email verification status through our wallet infrastructure provider."],[{text:"Profile information.",strong:!0}," Your username, bio, profile image and banner, and the network you choose."],[{text:"Content.",strong:!0}," Posts, replies, likes, reposts, quotes, bookmarks, polls and votes, stories, images and videos you upload, and messages you send in chats, communities, Spaces and live streams."],[{text:"Direct messages.",strong:!0}," The content of your direct messages and their metadata."],[{text:"Private notes.",strong:!0}," Notes you choose to save in features such as the memory vault."],[{text:"Security settings.",strong:!0}," If you turn them on, a two-factor authentication secret (stored encrypted), recovery codes and app lock PIN (stored as one-way hashes), and a recovery email address (stored as a one-way hash with a partially hidden copy for display)."],[{text:"Support and applications.",strong:!0}," Information you send us in support requests, reports, appeals and applications, for example tip listing applications."])),c("2. Information about your wallet and on-chain activity",s([{text:"Wallet addresses.",strong:!0}," The public addresses of the wallet made available to you when you sign in, and any other addresses you link."],[{text:"On-chain activity.",strong:!0}," Transactions involving your addresses on public blockchains, such as ticket purchases and sales, tips, swaps, transfers and token holdings. This information is public on the blockchain and can be seen by anyone."],[{text:"Trading activity.",strong:!0}," Orders, positions and fills on Hyperliquid made through the Services, and whether you choose to show your trading activity on your profile."]),i({text:"We never receive or store your wallet's private key or seed phrase.",strong:!0}," Your key is handled by our wallet infrastructure provider and is used on your own device.")),c("3. Information collected automatically",s([{text:"Device and log data.",strong:!0}," IP address, browser and device type, operating system, pages viewed, actions taken, referring pages and dates and times. Some security and fraud prevention records store a shortened IP address; others, such as referral and account recovery records, may store the full IP address."],[{text:"Cookies and similar technologies.",strong:!0}," We use a secure session cookie to keep you signed in, short lived cookies during sign-in, a referral cookie (up to 30 days), a cookie that counts anonymous live stream viewers, and browser local storage to remember your session, settings and selected network. These are needed for the Services to work."],[{text:"Analytics.",strong:!0}," We use Google Analytics to understand how the Services are used. Google Analytics uses its own cookies and collects information such as pages visited, device and approximate location. You can opt out with the ",{text:"Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on",href:"https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"},"."],[{text:"Push notifications.",strong:!0}," If you allow notifications, we store the subscription details your browser gives us to deliver them."])),c("4. How we use information",i("We use personal information to:"),s("provide, operate and maintain the Services, including your profile, feed, messages, communities, Spaces, live streams, wallet interface, tickets, tips, swaps and trading features;","authenticate you and keep accounts secure, including two-factor authentication, app lock and account recovery;","detect, investigate and prevent fraud, abuse, spam, security incidents and violations of our Terms, and to moderate content;","run points, badges, referral and reward programs, and prevent abuse of them;","send you security emails and, if you allow them, push notifications;","understand how the Services are used and improve them;","comply with law, respond to lawful requests and protect the rights, property and safety of BOI, our users and others."),i("Where the law of the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom applies, we rely on these legal bases: performance of our contract with you, our legitimate interests (such as security, fraud prevention, moderation and improving the Services), compliance with legal obligations, and your consent where we ask for it (for example push notifications).")),c("5. What is public",i("The following is visible to other users and, in many cases, to anyone on the internet: your profile (username, profile image, banner, bio, X handle and follower counts), your posts and other public content, your followers and following, your ticket holdings and holders, leaderboards and rankings you appear in, your trading activity if you choose to show it, and everything recorded on a public blockchain. Others can copy, share or save public content, and on-chain records cannot be deleted by anyone.")),c("6. How we share information",i("We do not sell your personal information for money. We share personal information only as described here:"),s([{text:"Service providers",strong:!0}," that host and run the Services for us, including Supabase (database and file storage), Vercel (hosting), Web3Auth (wallet and sign-in infrastructure, which receives your sign-in details including your X profile information), Google (analytics), Resend (security emails), our live audio and video infrastructure, a third-party data provider we use to read public X follower counts, and Telegram (internal operational alerts)."],[{text:"Blockchains and protocols you use.",strong:!0}," When you make a transaction, your wallet address and transaction details are sent to the relevant blockchain and to the protocols and providers that process it, such as Hyperliquid for trading and LI.FI for swaps and bridges, and to blockchain data and price providers."],[{text:"Card purchase provider.",strong:!0}," Where card purchases are offered and you choose to use them, we share with our provider, MoonPay, your wallet address, the selected asset and amount, the email address from your verified sign-in, a hashed form of your IP address and internal reference numbers. MoonPay collects your identity and payment information directly under its own privacy policy, and sends us the status, amount and country of your purchase."],[{text:"Embedded content.",strong:!0}," When you view embedded content such as YouTube or SoundCloud players, TradingView charts, GIFs, link previews, NFT images or profile images loaded from third parties, those providers may receive your IP address and browser information under their own policies."],[{text:"Other users.",strong:!0}," Content you send to other users, such as direct messages, is shared with them."],[{text:"Legal and safety.",strong:!0}," When we believe it is required by law, legal process or a government request, or needed to enforce our Terms, prevent fraud or harm, or protect the rights, property or safety of BOI, our users or others."],[{text:"Business changes.",strong:!0}," In connection with a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization, change of name or brand, or sale of all or part of our business or assets, in which case this Privacy Policy continues to apply to your information."],[{text:"With your consent",strong:!0}," or at your direction."])),c("7. Direct messages",i("Direct messages are not end-to-end encrypted. They are stored on our service providers' servers and may be accessed by us to investigate reports, enforce our Terms, keep the Services safe or comply with law. Images and videos you attach to messages or posts are stored as files that can be reached by anyone who has their link. Do not send information you need to keep secret.")),c("8. International transfers",i("BOI is a United States company. Our database is hosted in the European Union, and our service providers process information in the United States and other countries. These countries may have data protection laws that differ from those where you live. Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards for these transfers.")),c("9. Retention",i("We keep personal information for as long as your account is active and as needed to provide the Services, keep them secure, resolve disputes, enforce our agreements and meet legal obligations. Some records are deleted automatically, such as rate limiting records after about 48 hours and temporary sign-in records after about one hour. When you delete a post, story or message, it is removed from the Services, but copies may remain for a limited time in backups, logs and stored media files. Information recorded on a public blockchain cannot be deleted.")),c("10. Security",i("We use technical and organizational measures designed to protect personal information, including encryption in transit, encryption or one-way hashing of sensitive security factors, secure session cookies and access controls. No system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee the security of information you send to us. You are responsible for keeping your sign-in methods, devices and wallet secure.")),c("11. Your choices and rights",s("You can edit your profile, delete your posts, stories and messages, change your privacy settings, turn off push notifications and turn security features on or off 